modifications. This license applies only to rights the licensor can grant.

2. Preserve notices

When redistributing the Software, an adaptation, or a substantial portion
of its code, include this complete license, the copyright notice above,
and the original-project URL. Keep those notices with both source and
executable distributions. A standalone HTML distribution may carry them
in an embedded license-text block instead of a separate file.

3. Accessible interface attribution

If an application, website, or tool uses the Software or a substantial
portion of its code and has a graphical user interface, it must display
the following attribution in an About, Credits, Acknowledgements, or
equivalent section that users can easily reach from the main interface:

    Based on SimplePrompt

The attribution must link to:
    https://github.com/AlexZBA/SimplePrompt

This requirement applies to modified versions, commercial versions,
hosted services, and software combined into a larger product. It applies
to desktop and mobile layouts alike. Opening that section through a
clearly labelled, ordinary menu or button is sufficient. No permanent
attribution on the homepage, main screen, or main-interface footer is
required. Once the section is opened, the attribution must be readable,
and must not be concealed, made transparent, or obscured. Other credits
may appear alongside it. Attribution only in source comments or a
developer-only file does not satisfy this graphical-interface requirement.

If clickable links are technically unavailable, display the attribution
and the full original-project URL as readable text in that section.
Software without a graphical user interface must instead include them
in its ordinary help/about output or accompanying user documentation.

These obligations apply when distributing the covered code or making a
covered application available for use. They do not require attribution
on prompts, images, or other ordinary outputs produced with the tool.
Merely using the tool does not make those outputs covered code.

4. Other terms and third-party material

Additional terms for your own contributions must not remove the notice
and interface-attribution obligations for the covered Software. Nothing
here requires the public release of an adaptation's code. Credit must not
suggest that AlexZBA endorses an adaptation or its operator.

Third-party tag data, translations, artwork, dependencies, and other
third-party material are not relicensed by this document. Their applicable
rights, notices, and license terms remain separate. This license does not
grant trademark rights or rights in material the licensor does not own.

